{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent nonauthor per-block review receipt for merged Gerrit 3086 revision b10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63. All 67 selected prose blocks PASS semantic preservation, strict bloat removal, and directive checks. All 33 grouped reviewed file blobs match the approved candidate.\n\n```tsv\nticket\tstable_block_id\tbefore_citation\tfinal_citation\tpreserved_contract_or_consumer\tdirectives_exact\tbefore_words\tafter_words\tsemantic-preservation\tbloat-removal\treviewer_session\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py#D:<module>\tName optional compaction in write-lock timeout diagnostics.  The sweep stamps an ambient ``op=compact-sweep`` label. Timeouts render it with the safe-interrupt remedy while v2 stamps stay colon-free, unknown fields remain tolerated, and reclamation ignores the label.\tPASS\t118\t40\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py#D:<module>\tRetry a timed-out lock acquisition before the write body runs.  Bounded backoff covers a holder that outlives one acquire budget without duplicating a write. The retry belongs inside ``acquire()``, ahead of the caller's mutation.\tPASS\t144\t36\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_raise_errno\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_raise_errno\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_raise_errno\tOnly contention errno values wait for the deadline. Other lock-kernel errors propagate immediately and close the fd, including on Windows.\tPASS\t115\t21\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_tracker_and_symlink\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_tracker_and_symlink\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_tracker_and_symlink\tCanonical tracker paths make symlink and resolved-path callers contend on the same lock. A held first acquire forces the bounded second acquire to time out.\tPASS\t118\t26\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_seed_owner_stamp\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_seed_owner_stamp\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:_seed_owner_stamp\tReclaim only a stamp proving a dead local owner. Missing, malformed, unreadable, or foreign-host stamps cannot prove that claim.\tPASS\t50\t20\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:test_default_write_lock_takes_both_fcntl_and_mkdir_legs\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:test_default_write_lock_takes_both_fcntl_and_mkdir_legs\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py#C:<module>:before:test_default_write_lock_takes_both_fcntl_and_mkdir_legs\tDefault acquires both kernel and mkdir lock legs. ``dual_window=False`` deliberately selects only the kernel leg.\tPASS\t71\t16\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084.py#D:<module>\tReport the existing lock-owner stamp on timeout.  Diagnostics include holder identity and corroborated liveness, or name an absent, unrecognized, or incomplete stamp without guessing. Contended lock acquisition exercises the same path.\tPASS\t117\t32\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_main_health_report.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py#D:<module>\tGive scheduled main-health failures an actionable commit range.  A red run may cover multiple mirrored-main commits, so the rendered summary must identify the last green bound and a runnable bisect even while the run itself is failing.\tPASS\t123\t39\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_make_lint_hygiene_wiring.py#D:<module>\tKeep raw-git and wall-clock hygiene checks in local ``make lint``.  Both scripts also run in CI. The Makefile wiring prevents a local green gate from missing either check.\tPASS\t94\t30\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py#D:<module>\tCount one anchored observability marker per error.  Journald ingests stdout and stderr. The fail-safe stderr print owns the line-start token. Configured logging emits only the body. Subprocess tests count combined streams with and without logging configured.\tPASS\t160\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py#D:<module>\tCap each model request at its resolved output-token ceiling.  A config floor raised for a larger model can reach a later smaller-model call. The config seam may preserve that floor, but the wire request must not exceed the smaller model's cap and trigger a guaranteed provider rejection.\tPASS\t304\t50\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_concurrent_reclone_is_not_interleaved\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_concurrent_reclone_is_not_interleaved\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_concurrent_reclone_is_not_interleaved\tSerialize re-clones on the mounted tracker directory's inode.      A lock beside the volume would be private to each container and permit     interleaved clear-and-clone operations.\tPASS\t131\t28\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_failing_code_clone_surfaces_but_does_not_stop_the_container_booting\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_failing_code_clone_surfaces_but_does_not_stop_the_container_booting\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_failing_code_clone_surfaces_but_does_not_stop_the_container_booting\tReport a code-clone failure while continuing ticket ensure and container boot.      The missing code root must not be reported as fully provisioned. The healthy     tracker isolates the failure to the code clone.\tPASS\t137\t33\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone\tRecheck HEAD under the store lock before clearing a purportedly bad clone.      A peer may make it healthy after the first probe but before this worker gets     the lock. The ordered handoff proves the second probe matters.\tPASS\t163\t37\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_ensure_step_does_not_run_while_a_peer_holds_the_store_lock\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_ensure_step_does_not_run_while_a_peer_holds_the_store_lock\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_ensure_step_does_not_run_while_a_peer_holds_the_store_lock\tKeep the ensure helper under the same lock as clear-and-clone.      It creates lock files inside the store. A peer clone or clear would conflict.     Assert the helper is not invoked while the peer holds the lock.\tPASS\t161\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_so_attested_gates_can_resolve_main\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_so_attested_gates_can_resolve_main\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_so_attested_gates_can_resolve_main\tProvision a code repository with ``origin/main`` for attested gates.      The image copies source without ``.git``. A healthy tracker isolates this     test's observed clone to the code root.\tPASS\t170\t29\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_an_absent_code_mount_point_is_announced_and_skipped_not_failed\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_an_absent_code_mount_point_is_announced_and_skipped_not_failed\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_an_absent_code_mount_point_is_announced_and_skipped_not_failed\tSkip an absent code mount with a diagnostic, without creating its path.      A bare image or repair run may lack that volume. A mis-set path must not     receive an unplanned clone.\tPASS\t131\t32\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_poisoned_store_with_dot_git_but_no_resolvable_head_is_cleared_and_recloned\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_poisoned_store_with_dot_git_but_no_resolvable_head_is_cleared_and_recloned\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_poisoned_store_with_dot_git_but_no_resolvable_head_is_cleared_and_recloned\tAn existing ``.git`` with unresolvable HEAD is poisoned, not provisioned.      Clear and re-clone it so the persistent volume cannot serve an empty tracker.\tPASS\t83\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_even_without_a_tickets_pat\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_even_without_a_tickets_pat\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_even_without_a_tickets_pat\tClone the read-only code root even when the tickets PAT is blank.      ``REBAR_ROOT`` is always exported, and the code clone needs no tickets     credential. A healthy tracker distinguishes its ``main`` clone from tickets.\tPASS\t184\t34\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_no_pat_skips_the_clone_but_still_converges_the_store\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_no_pat_skips_the_clone_but_still_converges_the_store\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:test_no_pat_skips_the_clone_but_still_converges_the_store\tWithout a tickets PAT, skip that clone but still run the store ensure step.      The anonymous code checkout is independent of the tickets credential.\tPASS\t104\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#D:<module>\tExercise MCP entrypoint provisioning by running ``--provision-only``.  A stub git records operations on healthy, poisoned, missing, and contended stores. Liveness markers keep absence assertions from passing after an early script failure.\tPASS\t164\t32\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#C:<module>:before:_FLOCK_SHIM\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#C:<module>:before:_FLOCK_SHIM\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py#C:<module>:before:_FLOCK_SHIM\tUse system ``flock(1)`` where present. A macOS fallback locks the inherited fd with fcntl so the shell's open description keeps the lock after shim exit.\tPASS\t97\t27\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_status_populates_verified_at_sha:before:signature-read\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_status_populates_verified_at_sha:before:signature-read\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_status_populates_verified_at_sha:before:signature-read\tThe signed op-cert manifest is a list. Read verified_at_sha from its pinned verified-at-sha step. Treating it as a dict left the value unset. A faithful verdict avoids signing and SSH setup here.\tPASS\t63\t35\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_status_reports_stale_for_a_reopened_attestation:before:signature-read\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_status_reports_stale_for_a_reopened_attestation:before:signature-read\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_status_reports_stale_for_a_reopened_attestation:before:signature-read\tA reopened completion attestation is stale even when its signature verifies. compute_validity, as in plan_review_status, reports stale-reopened instead of treating the bare verified flag as current.\tPASS\t62\t27\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_start_preserves_graph_tristate_and_variant_key:before:llm-import\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_start_preserves_graph_tristate_and_variant_key:before:llm-import\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_verify_completion_start_preserves_graph_tristate_and_variant_key:before:llm-import\tKeep graph=None. Ticket-type defaults make epics verify their whole subtree. Converting it to False also changes the de-dup key, preventing async start and sync verification from sharing a run.\tPASS\t89\t32\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_follower_start_does_not_reclobber_the_leaders_index_record:before:mcp-import\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_follower_start_does_not_reclobber_the_leaders_index_record:before:mcp-import\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_follower_start_does_not_reclobber_the_leaders_index_record:before:mcp-import\tA follower attaches without writing the last-writer-wins index. A new running record could overwrite the leader's terminal result. Count writes while the leader is blocked to verify the follower records nothing.\tPASS\t68\t34\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_follower_poll_before_leader_index_write_reports_attaching:before:registry-reset\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_follower_poll_before_leader_index_write_reports_attaching:before:registry-reset\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_follower_poll_before_leader_index_write_reports_attaching:before:registry-reset\tA follower shares the leader's job_id without an index write. Before the leader writes running, the shared registry must report attaching, not unknown.\tPASS\t48\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_gate_status_includes_durable_unknown_when_the_durable_read_raises:before:boom\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_gate_status_includes_durable_unknown_when_the_durable_read_raises:before:boom\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py#C:test_gate_status_includes_durable_unknown_when_the_durable_read_raises:before:boom\tA recorded completion job with ticket_id carries durable. If its read raises, report unknown with a reason and retain the field.\tPASS\t42\t21\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py#D:<module>\tMCP gate resolvers raise ConfigError for unreadable config (8408).  Ruling 39f8-ae7c requires mcp_readonly and mcp_gate to name the gate and chain the parse fault, even when a safe default exists. The MCP envelope marks config_unreadable so callers can handle it (change 2045 PS4).\tPASS\t102\t44\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py#D:<module>\tA health response reports whether this container served an MCP initialize request.  The health route bypasses auth and DNS-rebinding guards. Autodeploy once promoted a container 54 seconds before its first MCP request. A wrong allowed hostname could return health 200 while MCP traffic got 421 (vaccinated-flavorous-solenodon).  The server drives initialize through its running StreamableHTTPSessionManager inside ASGI lifespan, before startup.complete lets uvicorn accept connections. Health reports the handshake result. The probe must use the HTTP request path and be bounded so failure or a hang cannot wedge startup. Each test proves the drive ran, then checks its result. Success and refusal are both covered.\tPASS\t254\t107\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py#D:test_run_http_with_grace_hands_uvicorn_an_app_that_runs_the_handshake\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py#D:test_run_http_with_grace_hands_uvicorn_an_app_that_runs_the_handshake\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py#D:test_run_http_with_grace_hands_uvicorn_an_app_that_runs_the_handshake\tCheck production wiring. Uvicorn receives the app whose lifespan runs the     handshake. A fake Config/Server avoids a port. Driving the captured app through     raw ASGI lifespan catches a missing install call that helper tests would miss.\tPASS\t65\t37\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_a_removed_load_bearing_input_fails_hard_instead_of_being_reported\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_a_removed_load_bearing_input_fails_hard_instead_of_being_reported\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_a_removed_load_bearing_input_fails_hard_instead_of_being_reported\tRemovedInputError escapes the health probe. Ordinary resolution faults are     reported as degraded to avoid healthcheck crash loops. A retired but set     TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR instead means the server may read an unexpected store.     Reporting it as absent would hide that misconfiguration. The explicit     propagation also guards against a future broader exception handler.\tPASS\t131\t50\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_boot_sweep_warns_naming_the_path_when_the_store_is_absent\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_boot_sweep_warns_naming_the_path_when_the_store_is_absent\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_boot_sweep_warns_naming_the_path_when_the_store_is_absent\tBoot continues when the store is missing, but warns with the checked path.     Silence alongside the old health response hid a storeless deployment. The     path makes the warning actionable.\tPASS\t87\t29\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_autodeploy_gate_names_the_storeless_refusal\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_autodeploy_gate_names_the_storeless_refusal\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:test_autodeploy_gate_names_the_storeless_refusal\tRequire a greppable refusal marker.      The script harness tests promotion with a missing expected store, no expected     store, and a legacy health body. This avoids pinning the shell predicate's spelling.\tPASS\t91\t31\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py#D:<module>\tHealth reports whether the ticket store is present and expected.  The route once reported only in_flight, so both the container healthcheck and blue-green readiness gate accepted a server with no store. Boot sweep was also silent (kilted-nuclear-bronco / mobile-groovy-badger). Health reports rather than fails. A missing store is a fault when a tracker directory was configured. Otherwise expected is false. Readiness uses these fields so deploying before store provisioning does not mark a serving container unhealthy.\tPASS\t216\t80\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py#D:<module>\tDe-duplicate concurrent MCP plan and completion gate calls (d80d).  A client may time out after 60 seconds while a billable gate lasting 15 to 20 minutes keeps running. Repeating the same gate/ticket/basis should share one computation. Event-blocked fakes count calls deterministically without LLM tokens. The registry joins threads because MCP runs synchronous tools on anyio workers and the in-flight gauge and shutdown drain depend on synchronous bodies.\tPASS\t192\t72\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py#D:<module>\tCheck that MCP gate tools use the in-flight registry (d80d).  The registry has separate tests. These exercise FastMCP review_plan and verify_completion on worker threads. An event-blocked fake counts underlying billable gate calls. Concurrent calls for one ticket must invoke it once.\tPASS\t93\t43\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py#C:test_two_concurrent_calls_invoke_the_gate_exactly_once:before:follower_attached\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py#C:test_two_concurrent_calls_invoke_the_gate_exactly_once:before:follower_attached\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py#C:test_two_concurrent_calls_invoke_the_gate_exactly_once:before:follower_attached\tRelease the leader after a waiting follower reaches _await_follower. A fixed sleep races the first CallTool's cold setup. If de-dup breaks, the second call becomes a leader. The bounded fallback releases both and calls == 2 fails instead of hanging.\tPASS\t92\t41\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_entrypoint_does_not_block_boot_on_the_tickets_clone\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_entrypoint_does_not_block_boot_on_the_tickets_clone\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_entrypoint_does_not_block_boot_on_the_tickets_clone\tClone the large tickets branch after exec so the server can answer health.      A pre-exec clone exceeded MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=120s and rolled back deployments     as mcp-unhealthy (unfit-beneficial-whimbrel). Review-bot has no such readiness     deadline. This structural check pins nonblocking entrypoint control flow.     Provisioning behavior runs in test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py.\tPASS\t148\t51\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_metadata_route_does_not_shadow_the_acme_challenge\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_metadata_route_does_not_shadow_the_acme_challenge\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_metadata_route_does_not_shadow_the_acme_challenge\tKeep certbot's HTTP-01 webroot route intact.      An exact metadata match leaves the ACME prefix alone. A broad     /.well-known/ location could break renewal.\tPASS\t53\t25\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_mcp_sets_both_bedrock_region_vars\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_mcp_sets_both_bedrock_region_vars\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_mcp_sets_both_bedrock_region_vars\tSet both MCP Bedrock region variables as the review-bot does.      Without them, boto3 has no region even with IMDS available (a574, 9249).     Rebar's region reaches BedrockProvider and signed provenance.     AWS_DEFAULT_REGION supplies bare boto3 callers.\tPASS\t93\t36\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_template_substitutes_cleanly_under_envsubst\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_template_substitutes_cleanly_under_envsubst\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_template_substitutes_cleanly_under_envsubst\tOnly REVIEW_BOT_PORT is substituted. Any other ${...} would survive     into deployed config and cause nginx to reject it.\tPASS\t34\t17\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_on_the_sibling_surfaces\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_on_the_sibling_surfaces\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_on_the_sibling_surfaces\tEvery /review/, /opcert/, and Gerrit TLS location upgrades http     Location headers from both forwarded-Host and upstream-address forms.\tPASS\t82\t19\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_sibling_surfaces_restate_the_default_proxy_redirect\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_sibling_surfaces_restate_the_default_proxy_redirect\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_sibling_surfaces_restate_the_default_proxy_redirect\tKeep proxy_redirect default first in each sibling location.      An explicit redirect rule disables nginx's implicit default. The review     upstream's prefix-stripping proxy_pass needs that default to restore /review/     on loopback Location headers. Rule order decides the first match.\tPASS\t105\t40\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_bluegreen_refreshes_ssm_secrets_before_starting_the_new_container\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_bluegreen_refreshes_ssm_secrets_before_starting_the_new_container\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_bluegreen_refreshes_ssm_secrets_before_starting_the_new_container\tRefresh SSM secrets before starting the new MCP container.      The rsync-excluded .env and mcp-static-tokens.json are materialized from SSM.     Rotating SecureString does not move git. On 2026-08-25, missing refresh left     three new PATs absent, nine blue-green retries failed auth, and the alarm     fired (receptive-houndy-nilgai). A refresh failure must leave the old     container serving, as on the review-bot path.\tPASS\t192\t67\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_serves_the_documented_mcp_slash_url_without_redirecting\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_serves_the_documented_mcp_slash_url_without_redirecting\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_serves_the_documented_mcp_slash_url_without_redirecting\tServe /mcp/ directly through exact-match locations for it and /mcp.      proxy_pass must include the app's /mcp path so Starlette cannot redirect or     produce a downgradeable Location header. A prefix location alone misses this.\tPASS\t81\t35\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_gerrit_location_still_has_no_rewrite_and_no_proxy_pass_path\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_gerrit_location_still_has_no_rewrite_and_no_proxy_pass_path\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_gerrit_location_still_has_no_rewrite_and_no_proxy_pass_path\tPreserve Gerrit's raw %2F-safe request URI.      Its location must have no rewrite and no proxy_pass URI component.     proxy_redirect changes only response Location/Refresh headers.\tPASS\t75\t26\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_asserts_hsts_on_every_tls_response\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_asserts_hsts_on_every_tls_response\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_asserts_hsts_on_every_tls_response\tServe HSTS with always, including unauthenticated 401 responses.      Without always, nginx omits add_header on errors, precisely when a new     client may first reach MCP.\tPASS\t53\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_from_the_mcp_upstream\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_from_the_mcp_upstream\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_from_the_mcp_upstream\tUpgrade any MCP upstream http Location to https at the edge.      Rules cover forwarded-Host and upstream-address forms in each MCP location.     They stay location-scoped. Server-level rules would replace proxy_redirect     default on /review/ and /opcert/, risking their relative redirects.\tPASS\t131\t42\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:_render_nginx\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:_render_nginx\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:_render_nginx\tRender the deployed template with only REVIEW_BOT_PORT substituted.      This matches envsubst without requiring gettext in CI and preserves nginx's     other variables while tests inspect the configuration nginx actually parses.\tPASS\t72\t30\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_location_restores_the_review_prefix_on_absolute_redirects\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_location_restores_the_review_prefix_on_absolute_redirects\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_location_restores_the_review_prefix_on_absolute_redirects\tRestore /review/ on same-host absolute review-bot redirects.      The rendered rule maps https://$host/<route> to     https://$host/review/<route>. Without it clients fall through to Gerrit 404.\tPASS\t78\t29\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_review_bot_redirect_surface_is_same_app_only\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_review_bot_redirect_surface_is_same_app_only\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_review_bot_redirect_surface_is_same_app_only\tGuard the broad same-host /review/ prefix rewrite (4d8c).      It is safe while review-bot's only absolute redirects are Starlette     trailing-slash redirects to its own routes. No root_path, redirect_slashes     override, or cross-route RedirectResponse may silently change that premise.\tPASS\t118\t41\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_mcp_trusts_the_edge_forwarded_proto\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_mcp_trusts_the_edge_forwarded_proto\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_mcp_trusts_the_edge_forwarded_proto\tTrust nginx's forwarded HTTPS scheme inside the MCP container (fernlike-toothsome-hen).      The docker bridge gateway, not default-trusted 127.0.0.1, connects to uvicorn.     Otherwise it emits http absolute URLs. Trust-all is bounded by the port's     host-loopback publication and nginx's literal X-Forwarded-Proto override.\tPASS\t175\t52\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_sibling_services_trust_the_edge_forwarded_proto\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_sibling_services_trust_the_edge_forwarded_proto\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_compose_sibling_services_trust_the_edge_forwarded_proto\tReview-bot and opcert trust nginx's forwarded HTTPS scheme (a61d).      The bridge gateway is not uvicorn's default-trusted 127.0.0.1, so without     FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS their absolute URLs, including slash redirects, use http.     Use * because the implicit gateway can drift. Host-loopback ports and nginx's     literal X-Forwarded-Proto override bound the trust.\tPASS\t183\t56\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:_location_body\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:_location_body\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:_location_body\tRead only directives in a brace-matched TLS location body.      Port-443 scoping avoids the port-80 redirect. Brace matching handles nested     if blocks. Strip comments so assertions cannot match a deleted directive     still named in its explanatory prose.\tPASS\t114\t39\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_entrypoint_is_a_real_file_installed_onto_path\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_entrypoint_is_a_real_file_installed_onto_path\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_mcp_entrypoint_is_a_real_file_installed_onto_path\tThe entrypoint is an installed file, as in Dockerfile.reviewbot.      Generating it inside Dockerfile RUN made execution tests impossible outside     the image. tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py now drives the file     itself instead of relying on source greps.\tPASS\t90\t37\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_prefix_restore_coexists_with_a61d_rules_default_first\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_prefix_restore_coexists_with_a61d_rules_default_first\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_prefix_restore_coexists_with_a61d_rules_default_first\tKeep the ordered redirect chain. Default first, then both a61d     http-to-https rules, then the same-host /review/ prefix restore.     nginx applies the first matching rule, so dropping or moving one regresses     an upstream form or scheme.\tPASS\t98\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_request_path_stays_prefix_stripping\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_request_path_stays_prefix_stripping\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_review_request_path_stays_prefix_stripping\tKeep request handling prefix-stripping. Trailing-slash proxy_pass maps     /review/health to app /health. The response-header redirect fix must not     change that path or mount the app under /review/.\tPASS\t75\t30\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_routes_the_advertised_resource_metadata_url_to_the_mcp_app\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_routes_the_advertised_resource_metadata_url_to_the_mcp_app\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#D:test_nginx_routes_the_advertised_resource_metadata_url_to_the_mcp_app\tRoute the advertised resource_metadata URL to MCP instead of Gerrit 404.      The rendered exact-match location passes the URI unchanged to the MCP     upstream, which answers it. A prefix could widen /.well-known/ routing.\tPASS\t87\t34\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_MCP_TICKETS_DIR\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_MCP_TICKETS_DIR\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_MCP_TICKETS_DIR\t--------------------------------------------------------------------------- ticket store MCP needs a writable external ticket-store volume. .dockerignore excludes the store and .git, so the image cannot contain it. The tracker-dir env points to that volume. The entrypoint clones tickets there. Missing PAT or failed clone defers provisioning without blocking boot, as in the review-bot canary.\tPASS\t122\t51\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_JIRA_PLAIN_LEAVES\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_JIRA_PLAIN_LEAVES\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_JIRA_PLAIN_LEAVES\tJira bridge credentials (colourless-hasteless-lamb). Without them, external bridge_check_access failed. URL, user, and project stay plain SSM Strings, as GitHub Actions vars and _child_env agree. Only the API token is SecureString. Missing outbound Jira credentials must leave MCP up, unlike missing bearer tokens. A blank slot cannot abort fetch-secrets.sh and lose the whole .env.\tPASS\t181\t57\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_server_443_block\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_server_443_block\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_server_443_block\tMCP edge downgrade regression (fernlike-toothsome-hen). /mcp/ returned a method-preserving 307 to http://<host>/mcp, risking bearer PAT disclosure. Exact-match routing must avoid Starlette's slash redirect, and uvicorn must trust nginx's forwarded HTTPS scheme. Both mechanisms are checked below.\tPASS\t152\t44\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_ADVERTISED_METADATA_PATH:routing\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_ADVERTISED_METADATA_PATH:routing\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_ADVERTISED_METADATA_PATH:routing\tMCP's 401 advertises a resource_metadata URL outside /mcp. The app served it directly, but the edge fell through to Gerrit 404 (71fe). Route that exact RFC 9728 path to MCP. The one advertised URL, exactly as it appears in the 401 `WWW-Authenticate` header.\tPASS\t76\t45\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:test_compose_mcp_trusts_the_edge_forwarded_proto:before:allow-ips-assert\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:test_compose_mcp_trusts_the_edge_forwarded_proto:before:allow-ips-assert\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:test_compose_mcp_trusts_the_edge_forwarded_proto:before:allow-ips-assert\tThe implicit bridge gateway can drift. A fixed address could silently restore the downgrade.\tPASS\t40\t14\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_SIBLING_SURFACES\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_SIBLING_SURFACES\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_SIBLING_SURFACES\tPrevent HTTP Location downgrades on all TLS surfaces (a61d). Review-bot and opcert received nginx from the docker bridge, outside uvicorn's default 127.0.0.1 trust, so slash redirects used http despite forwarded HTTPS. Gerrit uses an HTTPS canonicalWebUrl, but carries the edge backstop too. The three 443 surfaces that lacked the guarantee, with the upstream each proxies to. The upstream form is the second rule's left-hand side: an app can build an absolute Location either from the forwarded Host ($host) or from the upstream address it was reached on.\tPASS\t230\t94\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_REVIEW_BOT_DIR\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_REVIEW_BOT_DIR\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py#C:<module>:before:_REVIEW_BOT_DIR\tRestore /review/ on same-host absolute redirects (4d8c). The app runs at server root because proxy_pass strips the prefix. Its slash 307 redirects to https://<host>/<route>, which otherwise falls through to Gerrit 404. A location-scoped proxy_redirect restores /review/. nginx checks rules in Keep default first and a61d's http upgrades before this https rule.\tPASS\t192\t56\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\ninferior-mystical-arrowworm\ttests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py#D:<module>\t9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a:tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py#D:<module>\tVerify MCP op-certs signed by the box's trusted environment.  The server uses its env_id and materialized Ed25519 key. The merge gate checks the pinned public key. These tests use Ed25519 cryptography, a temporary store, and a fixture rebar.toml. Environment enforcement remains a deferred operator step (infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md).  AC1: a cert from the startup binding verifies. One from an unregistered key fails, without adding a pin or committing a private key. AC2: fixture require_environment and opcert_enforce_since reject an uncertified close after the boundary and grandfather one before it. AC3: removing require_environment restores advisory checks while an existing pinned cert still verifies.\tPASS\t238\t108\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group02:2026-10-23\n```"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792801868500121041,"uuid":"71cb2c6b-f109-4e78-b131-98df52f7586c"}